WEBVTT

00:00:00.440 --> 00:00:04.850
I asked Yuki to let me work 
with him for five years.

00:00:04.850 --> 00:00:06.560
Until the day the world ends,

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:10.710
you're the only partner in the universe 
that I want, now and forever.

00:00:11.470 --> 00:00:12.240
Really?

00:00:16.290 --> 00:00:17.300
Manager.

00:00:17.300 --> 00:00:18.290
What's after this?

00:00:18.290 --> 00:00:21.950
Yes. We have a meeting for the 
inaugural concert at Zero Arena.

00:00:23.790 --> 00:00:26.280
Apparently some new graffiti was found.

00:00:25.880 --> 00:00:26.880
<b>Zero Arena inaugural performance posters graffitied again 
Read more eyewitness accounts here</b>

00:00:26.880 --> 00:00:28.500
<b>Zero Arena inaugural performance posters graffitied again 
Read more eyewitness accounts here</b>

00:00:28.910 --> 00:00:33.260
Is the stress from the graffiti 
making Mr. Momo unable to sing?

00:00:33.550 --> 00:00:35.550
He shouldn't worry about this stuff.

00:00:35.930 --> 00:00:39.680
Yeah. There's no way it's Zero himself.

00:00:39.980 --> 00:00:43.980
Mitsuki-san, you met Zero when 
you were a child, didn't you?

00:00:44.250 --> 00:00:47.730
Yeah! He suddenly appeared 
in front of our store.

00:00:47.730 --> 00:00:50.450
It caused a huge fuss when
 everyone around noticed.

00:00:50.450 --> 00:00:54.780
But Zero danced for us without 
a single complaint.

00:00:55.070 --> 00:00:57.830
You were there, too, Iori. In your stroller.

00:00:58.250 --> 00:01:00.060
I don't remember that.

00:01:00.060 --> 00:01:02.330
It was like a dream...

00:01:02.710 --> 00:01:05.050
Why did he disappear?

00:01:05.050 --> 00:01:07.690
He's still missing, isn't he?

00:01:07.690 --> 00:01:09.920
It seems like there are a lot of theories.

00:01:09.920 --> 00:01:12.580
That he incurred the wrath of
 a major player in the industry,

00:01:12.580 --> 00:01:15.620
that the government tried 
to utilize his popularity,

00:01:15.620 --> 00:01:18.970
that he was erased because he 
was royalty from some country...

00:01:16.860 --> 00:01:17.720
Oh?

00:01:19.290 --> 00:01:22.970
A prince wouldn't bother becoming an idol.

00:01:23.790 --> 00:01:25.060
Yeah.

00:01:25.360 --> 00:01:27.350
Rokuya-san, do you know anything?

00:01:27.350 --> 00:01:31.070
Don't you know Sakura Haruki-san, 
who wrote Zero's songs?

00:01:31.300 --> 00:01:34.660
I don't know. Haruki didn't tell me anything.

00:01:34.660 --> 00:01:36.570
Perhaps he didn't know.

00:01:39.400 --> 00:01:41.080
Why Zero disappeared?

00:01:41.360 --> 00:01:44.020
Yes. If you know, I'd appreciate—

00:01:43.200 --> 00:01:45.720
If you're a fan of his, it's better not to know.

00:01:45.720 --> 00:01:48.210
Zero's best remembered 
according to his legend.

00:01:48.480 --> 00:01:50.000
What does that mean?

00:01:51.690 --> 00:01:56.260
The legendary idol Zero vanished because 
he was exposed to too many dreams.

00:01:57.040 --> 00:01:58.260
Dreams?

00:01:58.670 --> 00:02:03.280
Zero suddenly disappeared after 
his final legendary concert.

00:02:03.280 --> 00:02:08.150
Also, someone just happened to be transported
to the hospital from Zero Arena on that day.

00:02:08.150 --> 00:02:09.380
Could it be?

00:02:09.930 --> 00:02:12.660
As idols, you must understand 
how difficult it is

00:02:12.660 --> 00:02:18.040
to sing with the entire nation's attention 
and expectations weighing on you.

00:02:19.280 --> 00:02:22.460
Zero was probably too kind.

00:02:22.460 --> 00:02:25.820
He'd meet ten expectations 
and be asked for a hundred.

00:02:25.820 --> 00:02:29.460
When he delivered on a thousand, 
he'd be asked for ten million.

00:02:29.460 --> 00:02:31.740
He just broke.

00:02:31.740 --> 00:02:32.920
Do you have proof of that?

00:02:33.230 --> 00:02:37.880
If Zero's the one writing the graffiti 
around town, that would explain it.

00:02:38.380 --> 00:02:39.880
There's no way...

00:02:40.300 --> 00:02:41.390
Nii-san...

00:02:41.880 --> 00:02:45.390
Is Re:vale all right? What about Momo-kun?

00:02:48.900 --> 00:02:51.900
The brighter the light, 
the deeper the darkness.

00:02:52.970 --> 00:02:55.520
Take care of yourselves.

00:02:57.060 --> 00:02:59.900
Do you think what he said was true?

00:03:00.940 --> 00:03:02.360
I don't believe it.

00:03:03.670 --> 00:03:08.130
But if it's true, I wish he'd cheer up.

00:03:08.130 --> 00:03:11.260
I understand both the fear and 
sweetness of being pushed around

00:03:11.260 --> 00:03:12.570
by the voices of those around you.

00:03:12.570 --> 00:03:13.750
Mitsuki...

00:03:14.510 --> 00:03:16.920
What's going to happen to us?

00:03:17.490 --> 00:03:22.070
In one year—in five years, 
will anything have changed?

00:03:22.070 --> 00:03:27.340
Well, I think it would be all 
right if you changed a little.

00:03:27.340 --> 00:03:29.100
What's that supposed to mean?

00:03:29.100 --> 00:03:31.060
I meant exactly what I said.

00:03:31.060 --> 00:03:32.820
Cut it out.

00:03:32.820 --> 00:03:34.920
You guys are always arguing.

00:03:38.780 --> 00:03:40.870
I hope we can stay the same.

00:03:40.870 --> 00:03:44.530
Me, all of us, and all the people we've met.

00:03:45.130 --> 00:03:46.700
Always and forever.

00:03:46.700 --> 00:03:48.040
It's all right.

00:03:48.350 --> 00:03:52.040
No matter what happens, I'll protect you.

00:03:52.580 --> 00:03:54.820
You're precious idols.

00:03:54.820 --> 00:03:56.650
No matter who comes after you,

00:03:57.340 --> 00:04:00.010
I will protect you.

00:04:01.800 --> 00:04:02.810
Manager...

00:04:04.190 --> 00:04:08.220
If we don't do anything after that speech, 
we should be ashamed of ourselves.

00:04:08.470 --> 00:04:10.210
We'll do our best.

00:04:10.210 --> 00:04:14.060
We'll give your beloved 
IDOLiSH7 everything we've got!

00:04:14.060 --> 00:04:15.000
Thank you.

00:04:17.420 --> 00:04:19.510
Timed with the second day 
of the inaugural concert,

00:04:19.510 --> 00:04:22.370
you'll be releasing your second album!

00:04:22.370 --> 00:04:23.610
What?

00:04:23.950 --> 00:04:25.360
Our second album?

00:04:25.640 --> 00:04:27.910
Yes. We're planning to include a new song.

00:04:28.150 --> 00:04:31.070
Who's going to be the center?

00:04:31.070 --> 00:04:32.580
Rikkun or Iorin?

00:04:33.010 --> 00:04:33.760
I...

00:04:33.760 --> 00:04:34.760
I'll do it!

00:04:35.390 --> 00:04:36.360
I'd like to do it!

00:04:37.260 --> 00:04:38.290
Nanase-san...

00:04:38.290 --> 00:04:44.480
You helped me when we released our last 
song, but this time I'll fulfill my role.

00:04:44.480 --> 00:04:46.160
My condition has stabilized.

00:04:46.160 --> 00:04:48.320
I won't cause any more trouble for the group.

00:04:48.320 --> 00:04:49.800
Please let me do it!

00:04:51.600 --> 00:04:53.010
Of course!

00:04:53.010 --> 00:04:55.020
We're counting on you, Riku-san.

00:04:55.790 --> 00:04:56.560
Got it!

00:04:57.130 --> 00:05:00.370
Also, I have a suggestion.

00:05:00.370 --> 00:05:04.570
Before releasing the new song, 
I'd like to follow up with our fans.

00:05:05.080 --> 00:05:09.580
They may be shocked to learn Iori-san 
won't be the center anymore.

00:05:11.590 --> 00:05:16.190
Similarly, I'd like to reassure 
the fans who were startled

00:05:16.190 --> 00:05:18.380
after Riku-san was replaced as the center.

00:05:18.890 --> 00:05:21.870
I'd rather not tell them about my illness.

00:05:21.870 --> 00:05:24.630
I only want people to be 
happy when they see us.

00:05:25.120 --> 00:05:28.760
I believe your professionalism 
and desire not to reveal

00:05:28.760 --> 00:05:30.660
behind-the-scenes information is important.

00:05:30.660 --> 00:05:36.640
But I also believe communicating your 
concerns and honest feelings may reassure them.

00:05:37.170 --> 00:05:38.440
Reassure them?

00:05:38.440 --> 00:05:41.520
Even if it makes us seem 
pathetic or imperfect?

00:05:42.050 --> 00:05:44.040
What is perfect, anyway?

00:05:45.370 --> 00:05:48.410
Tenn-nii's... TRIGGER's concerts...

00:05:48.830 --> 00:05:54.120
Your fans don't want to see perfection. 
They want to see what makes you you.

00:05:54.120 --> 00:05:59.410
They've supported you until now because 
they like you the way you are.

00:06:00.330 --> 00:06:02.920
So, what exactly are we supposed to do?

00:06:03.320 --> 00:06:07.930
We'll respect Riku-san's wishes and 
not reveal his physical condition.

00:06:07.930 --> 00:06:08.930
Huh?

00:06:09.370 --> 00:06:12.680
Instead, please honestly convey your feelings

00:06:12.680 --> 00:06:17.080
to your fans during the next MC 
segment at your next concert.

00:06:28.950 --> 00:06:30.330
Thank you!

00:06:35.620 --> 00:06:37.300
Everyone, please have a seat.

00:06:37.300 --> 00:06:39.830
There's something we'd like to tell you.

00:06:48.530 --> 00:06:50.870
You make it sound so serious.

00:06:50.870 --> 00:06:52.860
It's just our usual MC segment.

00:06:52.860 --> 00:06:55.560
We'll be speaking for a while, 
so please have a seat.

00:06:57.770 --> 00:06:58.800
Uh...

00:07:00.600 --> 00:07:02.410
Where should I start?

00:07:02.410 --> 00:07:05.120
Iorin, you can do it!

00:07:07.670 --> 00:07:08.890
Thank you.

00:07:09.680 --> 00:07:11.730
As fans who have known 
IDOLiSH7 since before

00:07:11.730 --> 00:07:15.150
<i>Lovely Night With You </i>are already aware,

00:07:15.790 --> 00:07:18.250
our center used to be Nanase-san here.

00:07:18.730 --> 00:07:23.000
Due to certain circumstances, 
I became the center instead,

00:07:23.360 --> 00:07:26.420
but with our next song, Nanase-san 
will become the center again.

00:07:26.420 --> 00:07:28.010
What?!

00:07:28.660 --> 00:07:33.130
The past few months have been a 
valuable experience for me. Thank you.

00:07:33.480 --> 00:07:35.120
Great job!

00:07:35.120 --> 00:07:38.780
Also, Nanase-san is a spineless, 
unreliable, careless,

00:07:38.780 --> 00:07:43.210
and absent-minded person with a lot 
of flaws despite being older than me.

00:07:43.210 --> 00:07:43.770
Hey...

00:07:44.080 --> 00:07:50.280
But after becoming the center myself, 
I realized that Nanase-san is incredible.

00:07:51.780 --> 00:07:53.930
Like all of you—

00:07:53.930 --> 00:07:57.160
No, more than anyone here in this arena,

00:07:57.600 --> 00:08:00.910
I love Nanase-san's vocals.

00:08:03.610 --> 00:08:07.660
Nanase-san will exceed your 
expectations with our new song.

00:08:08.640 --> 00:08:10.520
Go ahead and announce it, then.

00:08:12.260 --> 00:08:14.900
You're always putting pressure on me.

00:08:14.900 --> 00:08:16.300
Please.

00:08:18.130 --> 00:08:20.070
I feel like we haven't talked 
like this in forever.

00:08:20.070 --> 00:08:21.700
It makes me happy.

00:08:23.610 --> 00:08:24.770
Uh...

00:08:25.520 --> 00:08:27.690
Nice to meet you. I'm Nanase Riku.

00:08:27.690 --> 00:08:29.940
Nice to meet you!

00:08:27.690 --> 00:08:29.940
They've met you before.

00:08:30.150 --> 00:08:32.920
Oh, right. Sorry.

00:08:32.920 --> 00:08:34.170
I'm Nanase Riku.

00:08:34.950 --> 00:08:38.100
I was actually a little anxious today.

00:08:38.640 --> 00:08:41.490
I was worried Iori's fans 
would be disappointed

00:08:41.490 --> 00:08:43.330
or that I wouldn't be able to sing well.

00:08:43.850 --> 00:08:48.460
But after standing onstage and seeing 
all your smiles, all that went away.

00:08:50.460 --> 00:08:52.600
I love our fans!

00:08:52.970 --> 00:08:53.970
Iori,

00:08:54.240 --> 00:08:55.220
Yamato-san,

00:08:55.520 --> 00:08:56.590
Mitsuki,

00:08:56.590 --> 00:08:57.970
Sogo-san,

00:08:57.970 --> 00:08:59.220
Nagi,

00:08:59.220 --> 00:09:00.560
and Tamaki.

00:09:00.560 --> 00:09:03.850
I love everyone!

00:09:06.330 --> 00:09:08.600
Our members are amazing.

00:09:08.600 --> 00:09:10.510
I could brag about them forever.

00:09:10.510 --> 00:09:13.420
I wish I could tell the world
 about our fans, too.

00:09:13.420 --> 00:09:16.420
Despite all the suspense and 
worry we've put you through,

00:09:16.420 --> 00:09:19.150
thanks for continuing to support us!

00:09:19.150 --> 00:09:20.760
Thank you!

00:09:24.090 --> 00:09:28.060
Your smiles were so kind, 
I nearly cried a bunch of times.

00:09:28.060 --> 00:09:30.580
Thank you so, so much!

00:09:32.390 --> 00:09:34.140
You can do it!

00:09:51.260 --> 00:09:54.980
I'll sing my heart out so 
Iori, the other members,

00:09:55.440 --> 00:09:59.160
and all our fans won't ever be sad again.

00:09:59.550 --> 00:10:03.650
I'll protect this special 
space I love so much!

00:10:05.170 --> 00:10:08.790
IDOLiSH7's new song is "RESTART POiNTER"!

00:10:09.670 --> 00:10:11.690
Rikkun, welcome back!

00:10:11.690 --> 00:10:14.170
We've been waiting for you!

00:10:18.730 --> 00:10:23.600
<i>I'm sure I'll remember this night 
every time I sing this song.</i>

00:10:28.860 --> 00:10:35.860
If I can smile with you,
we can change any day

00:10:35.860 --> 00:10:44.450
Let's dream a new dream again, 
Step on dream... Together

00:10:56.460 --> 00:11:03.300
There's something we can't see yet, 
the desire to want to know

00:11:03.300 --> 00:11:10.140
Shakes my heart from that day, like a yell

00:11:10.140 --> 00:11:17.170
I want to scream, but I'm a bit scared,
yet we should be able to take the step, right?

00:11:17.170 --> 00:11:23.870
Jump on and Glide! 
The certain Melody is still playing

00:11:24.110 --> 00:11:29.040
The person you should face is (Nowhere)

00:11:27.530 --> 00:11:33.290
Unreflected in your eyes (Come on)

00:11:31.080 --> 00:11:39.120
Once you decide, stick with it,
and we'll risk everything... Going on!

00:11:39.120 --> 00:11:46.100
Fly high! That's why I believe that
you should race through however you want

00:11:46.100 --> 00:11:53.020
No matter how many times, RESTART POiNT, 
carve your RESOLUTiON into your heart

00:11:53.020 --> 00:11:59.650
If I can smile with you, 
we can overcome any day

00:11:54.730 --> 00:11:56.850
<i>I love this moment.</i>

00:11:56.850 --> 00:12:01.710
<i>It lets me forget all my insignificant 
thoughts and reset my feelings.</i>

00:11:59.650 --> 00:12:09.290
Let's dream a new dream again, 
Step on dream... Together

00:12:01.710 --> 00:12:04.070
<i>It reminds me that this is where I belong.</i>

00:12:04.070 --> 00:12:06.780
<i>That there are things even I can do.</i>

00:12:06.780 --> 00:12:09.290
<i>That someone's always watching over me.</i>

00:12:09.720 --> 00:12:12.650
<i>That the things important 
to me are being recognized.</i>

00:12:12.650 --> 00:12:16.170
<i>Like returning to my sweet old hometown.</i>

00:12:16.980 --> 00:12:20.080
<i>That's why we can keep on singing.</i>

00:12:28.540 --> 00:12:30.930
Thank you, everyone!

00:12:30.930 --> 00:12:32.510
Thank you!

00:12:33.220 --> 00:12:35.300
Thank you!

00:12:37.120 --> 00:12:38.440
Ready, and...

00:12:38.440 --> 00:12:42.360
We love IDOLiSH7!

00:12:44.350 --> 00:12:46.450
Oof.

00:12:48.570 --> 00:12:50.630
That's a lot of letters.

00:12:50.630 --> 00:12:51.870
Good morning.

00:12:51.350 --> 00:12:52.540
Hey.

00:12:51.870 --> 00:12:53.000
Good morning.

00:12:53.250 --> 00:12:54.350
Good morning.

00:12:54.350 --> 00:12:55.000
Morning.

00:12:55.590 --> 00:12:56.340
Wow!

00:12:56.340 --> 00:12:59.130
Oh! Are these all fan letters?

00:12:59.130 --> 00:13:04.170
Yes. This might be the first time we've 
received this big a response after a concert.

00:13:04.380 --> 00:13:07.340
There was the surprise 
announcement of the new song,

00:13:07.340 --> 00:13:12.430
but I think creating a historic sense of unity
 between the members and fans was good.

00:13:12.650 --> 00:13:16.560
Your fans must have sensed the trust 
between Riku-san and Iori-san.

00:13:16.560 --> 00:13:17.880
All right!

00:13:17.880 --> 00:13:20.760
Let's practice hard again today!

00:13:20.760 --> 00:13:23.430
Yes! We'll keep on fighting!

00:13:23.430 --> 00:13:27.740
Hey, you guys are back to your usual
 positive and hot-blooded selves.

00:13:36.580 --> 00:14:02.940
<b>Is IDOLiSH7 appropriating Zero's songs?!</b>

00:13:36.860 --> 00:13:40.260
<i>What? Is i7 using Zero's songs
 without his permission?</i>

00:13:40.260 --> 00:13:42.590
<i>Isn't that why Zero got mad 
and graffitied those posters?</i>

00:13:42.590 --> 00:13:46.430
<i>If Zero himself doesn't like it, 
they shouldn't cover his song.</i>

00:13:46.090 --> 00:13:54.420
<b>Entertainment News! 
TopicTopic!!</b>

00:13:46.430 --> 00:13:48.710
<i>There seems to be a lot of 
criticism going around.</i>

00:13:48.710 --> 00:13:52.920
<i>People had already been talking 
about IDOLiSH7 because</i>

00:13:52.920 --> 00:13:54.830
<i>their songs are similar 
to Sakura Haruki's work.</i>

00:13:54.830 --> 00:13:58.150
<i>They were definitely 
written by Sakura Haruki.</i>

00:13:58.150 --> 00:14:03.300
<i>Their agency should hold a press 
conference soon and apologize.</i>

00:14:06.820 --> 00:14:08.680
Hello, this is Takanashi Productions.

00:14:09.170 --> 00:14:10.840
Yes. Yes.

00:14:11.290 --> 00:14:14.700
We are not accepting any questions 
concerning the composer.

00:14:14.700 --> 00:14:18.330
I'm sorry, but we're not answering any 
questions concerning the composer.

00:14:18.330 --> 00:14:20.830
My apologies, but we appreciate 
your understanding. Goodbye.

00:14:18.880 --> 00:14:20.830
Hello, this is Takanashi Productions.

00:14:21.160 --> 00:14:24.590
Yes, I'm sorry. We're not currently...

00:14:25.690 --> 00:14:28.190
All phone lines are currently in use.

00:14:28.190 --> 00:14:30.800
Your call cannot be completed.

00:14:30.800 --> 00:14:34.750
Ban-chan's finally pretending 
to be a recorded message...

00:14:34.750 --> 00:14:37.110
Why are people making a fuss over us?

00:14:37.110 --> 00:14:38.720
We're the victims here, aren't we?

00:14:38.720 --> 00:14:40.810
The world was already endlessly discussing

00:14:40.810 --> 00:14:45.690
Re:vale's cover of Zero's song and all
 the graffiti by someone resembling Zero.

00:14:45.690 --> 00:14:48.140
Then the message to "Haruki 
the Betrayer" showed up.

00:14:48.900 --> 00:14:52.320
Millions of detectives wanted 
to decipher the code.

00:14:52.320 --> 00:14:57.240
They arrived at the man who wrote 
songs for Zero, Sakura Haruki.

00:14:57.240 --> 00:14:59.410
And our songs closely resemble his.

00:14:59.410 --> 00:15:01.520
The timing was bad.

00:15:01.520 --> 00:15:04.060
It all came to light at a time 
when people feel like

00:15:04.060 --> 00:15:06.590
the legendary idol Zero 
should be left alone.

00:15:06.590 --> 00:15:12.120
By singing Sakura Haruki's songs, 
we're making Zero and his fans angry.

00:15:12.120 --> 00:15:13.430
That's what everyone believes.

00:15:13.660 --> 00:15:16.770
Did Zero really write that graffiti?

00:15:16.770 --> 00:15:17.940
Mitsuki...

00:15:17.940 --> 00:15:22.350
Is Zero angry that we're 
singing Sakura Haruki's songs?

00:15:22.660 --> 00:15:26.860
At the very least, whoever 
wrote that graffiti thinks so.

00:15:29.850 --> 00:15:31.190
I'm sorry.

00:15:31.190 --> 00:15:34.950
Because we were slow to respond, 
the rumors kept spreading.

00:15:35.260 --> 00:15:38.600
We've never been very good 
at handling the media.

00:15:40.390 --> 00:15:41.330
A guest...

00:15:41.990 --> 00:15:43.190
Don't open the door!

00:15:43.190 --> 00:15:44.130
Huh?

00:15:44.130 --> 00:15:46.000
Use the intercom.

00:15:47.490 --> 00:15:48.590
Understood.

00:15:49.560 --> 00:15:51.030
This is Takanashi Productions—

00:15:50.050 --> 00:15:52.430
<i>Could we get a comment regarding the graffiti?</i>

00:15:52.710 --> 00:15:54.960
<i>Do you believe it was 
written by Zero himself?</i>

00:15:54.960 --> 00:15:58.320
<i>Could you tell us about your 
relationship with Sakura Haruki-san?</i>

00:15:57.450 --> 00:15:59.720
I'm sorry. We can't answer 
those questions at this time.

00:16:00.930 --> 00:16:02.920
Yikes...

00:16:01.820 --> 00:16:04.770
Things may be worse than we thought.

00:16:09.040 --> 00:16:12.620
So-chan, that was pretty crazy earlier.

00:16:12.620 --> 00:16:16.500
When we left the office,
the media surrounded us, like, waah,

00:16:16.500 --> 00:16:19.050
and the manager drove up in a car, like, bam!

00:16:19.050 --> 00:16:22.680
Then we all piled in, like, whoosh! 
And then, like, vroom! Sped off.

00:16:19.480 --> 00:16:20.830
<i>What should I do?</i>

00:16:20.830 --> 00:16:24.630
<i>I still haven't told him about 
Aya-chan, and now this...</i>

00:16:22.710 --> 00:16:27.670
I'd only ever seen stuff like that on TV, 
but I guess it really happens.

00:16:29.720 --> 00:16:31.440
So-chan, are you listening?

00:16:32.430 --> 00:16:36.050
You look pale. Have you been 
pushing yourself too hard again?

00:16:33.830 --> 00:16:36.050
<i>What should I do? When should I tell him?</i>

00:16:36.050 --> 00:16:37.180
So-chan?

00:16:37.580 --> 00:16:40.140
What's wrong? Does your stomach hurt?

00:16:40.140 --> 00:16:43.440
I-It's nothing! I'm fine.

00:16:43.440 --> 00:16:47.060
So-chan, are you hiding something from me?

00:16:47.290 --> 00:16:48.820
N-No.

00:16:49.880 --> 00:16:51.010
Oh, really?

00:17:00.800 --> 00:17:01.720
Here.

00:17:03.600 --> 00:17:05.930
You seemed kind of tired.

00:17:06.370 --> 00:17:07.440
Thanks.

00:17:08.110 --> 00:17:09.720
Were things okay today?

00:17:12.410 --> 00:17:13.470
Sogo-san?

00:17:13.980 --> 00:17:17.010
Riku-kun, I'd like to tell you a story.

00:17:17.300 --> 00:17:18.430
A story?

00:17:18.640 --> 00:17:20.310
A traditional comedic story.

00:17:20.790 --> 00:17:26.880
A long time ago, in a certain part of Edo, 
Riku-kun and Kujo-kun worked as firemen.

00:17:26.880 --> 00:17:29.210
Tenn-nii and me as firemen, huh?

00:17:29.210 --> 00:17:31.210
Like those tough guys who say, 
"The hell you doin'?!"

00:17:31.210 --> 00:17:35.100
Yeah. But one day, Kujo-kun went missing.

00:17:35.100 --> 00:17:36.360
Tenn-nii went missing?

00:17:36.360 --> 00:17:40.240
Riku-kun was worried but 
continued working as a fireman.

00:17:40.570 --> 00:17:44.480
Then one day, Iori-kun the 
fireman found Kujo-kun.

00:17:44.950 --> 00:17:48.370
Kujo-kun told Iori-kun the following:

00:17:48.370 --> 00:17:49.920
"No matter what, I don't want Riku to—"

00:17:49.920 --> 00:17:52.270
This isn't much of a comedic story.

00:17:52.270 --> 00:17:54.170
Try speaking more like you're a fireman.

00:17:54.170 --> 00:17:54.940
What?

00:17:54.940 --> 00:17:58.380
"Th-The hell? I can't see Riku!"

00:17:58.380 --> 00:18:00.850
"You'd better not tell nobody about this!"

00:18:01.110 --> 00:18:03.080
What happened next?

00:18:03.080 --> 00:18:07.150
Before that, what did you 
think of the story so far?

00:18:07.150 --> 00:18:09.410
What do you think Iori-kun should do?

00:18:09.410 --> 00:18:11.770
Speak more like a fireman.

00:18:13.650 --> 00:18:19.280
What? Oh, I think Iori should ask 
Tenn-nii why he can't see me.

00:18:19.280 --> 00:18:21.240
He ran away before he could ask.

00:18:21.540 --> 00:18:24.000
That Iori sounds pretty useless.

00:18:24.000 --> 00:18:25.790
Why is he even in the story?

00:18:27.260 --> 00:18:28.970
Wh-What's wrong?

00:18:28.970 --> 00:18:30.960
Is this supposed to be a sad story?

00:18:30.960 --> 00:18:34.690
What do you think the 
useless Iori-kun should do?

00:18:34.690 --> 00:18:37.050
Do you think he should explain 
the situation to Riku-kun?

00:18:37.050 --> 00:18:38.800
Yes, I do.

00:18:38.800 --> 00:18:42.330
You don't think he'd neglect
his duties as a fireman?

00:18:42.330 --> 00:18:47.370
If he doesn't do his job, then Edo 
will be consumed by a sea of fire.

00:18:47.370 --> 00:18:49.430
This story suddenly got really serious!

00:18:50.850 --> 00:18:54.480
I think he'd feel restless, 
but he'd still do his job.

00:18:54.480 --> 00:18:56.640
I see. So I should tell—

00:18:56.640 --> 00:18:58.990
It'd be a different story
if it were Tamaki, though.

00:19:00.150 --> 00:19:01.550
Sogo-san?!

00:19:01.550 --> 00:19:06.700
Then what should the useless 
Iori-kun do in order to be useful?

00:19:06.700 --> 00:19:10.060
There's no way for the 
useless Iori to be useful.

00:19:10.060 --> 00:19:12.000
He doesn't need to be 
part of the story anymore.

00:19:14.750 --> 00:19:16.130
What's wrong, Iori?

00:19:16.650 --> 00:19:21.090
Nii-san, I... I think the other 
members might not like me.

00:19:21.090 --> 00:19:21.890
Huh?

00:19:24.410 --> 00:19:26.490
Yama-san, are you awake?

00:19:26.490 --> 00:19:27.140
Yeah.

00:19:27.140 --> 00:19:28.850
Hey.

00:19:28.850 --> 00:19:30.850
Don't you need to sleep, Tama?

00:19:30.850 --> 00:19:32.820
Don't you have an early 
morning shoot tomorrow?

00:19:32.820 --> 00:19:37.840
Yeah. So-chan's been acting weird lately.

00:19:37.840 --> 00:19:38.900
"Weird" how?

00:19:39.170 --> 00:19:43.730
He keeps complimenting me a bunch 
while his eyes dart around everywhere.

00:19:43.730 --> 00:19:45.740
I can imagine that.

00:19:45.740 --> 00:19:47.160
You don't have any idea why?

00:19:47.500 --> 00:19:52.080
Nope. But So-chan's worried 
about his family, y'know?

00:19:52.500 --> 00:19:55.210
If you're worried about him,
 you should just ask directly.

00:19:55.210 --> 00:19:58.080
So-chan won't tell me.

00:19:58.080 --> 00:20:00.700
What you told me was a lie, wasn't it?

00:20:00.700 --> 00:20:03.640
About him respecting me.

00:20:04.330 --> 00:20:05.390
Tama...

00:20:05.710 --> 00:20:11.120
It's fine. I've been terrible to him
 and caused a lot of trouble.

00:20:11.120 --> 00:20:13.870
I can't help if he doesn't trust me.

00:20:13.870 --> 00:20:15.400
That's not true.

00:20:15.400 --> 00:20:19.180
He always seems happy 
when you get praised.

00:20:19.180 --> 00:20:20.700
That's definitely true.

00:20:20.700 --> 00:20:24.960
I see. If he's not worried about 
his family, then that's fine.

00:20:24.960 --> 00:20:30.660
I told him before that he doesn't get it
 'cause he grew up in a normal family.

00:20:31.190 --> 00:20:33.540
But... things were tough for him, too.

00:20:33.540 --> 00:20:36.790
The uncle he loved died, and he 
was kicked out of the family.

00:20:37.130 --> 00:20:40.250
Tama, you're a good, kind guy.

00:20:40.250 --> 00:20:44.090
We all love that about you.

00:20:45.730 --> 00:20:46.430
Thanks.

00:20:46.800 --> 00:20:49.300
So's the type to carry everything on his own.

00:20:49.300 --> 00:20:53.240
When he's ready, he'll talk to you first.

00:20:53.810 --> 00:20:54.850
I dunno about that...

00:20:55.120 --> 00:20:57.760
Go to bed. Don't oversleep tomorrow.

00:20:57.760 --> 00:20:58.910
Goodnight.

00:21:04.270 --> 00:21:06.790
Is it okay for me to wait?

00:21:08.000 --> 00:21:10.680
<i>To trust him and wait?</i>

00:21:13.360 --> 00:21:14.910
#11 The Place I Want to Protect

00:21:14.910 --> 00:21:20.630
We came to understand a brilliant something

00:21:21.340 --> 00:21:26.840
resembling all the light in the galaxy

00:21:27.500 --> 00:21:39.230
Even on days I'm scared, the faint 
warmth I want to deliver won't disappear

00:21:39.230 --> 00:21:45.450
Even if you want to close your 
eyes to reality's reflection

00:21:45.450 --> 00:21:51.120
Come on, let's create an illusion

00:21:51.120 --> 00:21:53.540
The sound of the future

00:21:54.570 --> 00:21:57.790
On the curtain of three thousand worlds

00:21:57.790 --> 00:22:01.000
We quietly adorn

00:22:01.000 --> 00:22:06.160
Each and every one of us has meaning

00:22:06.760 --> 00:22:10.050
It's the message of the Fantasia

00:22:10.050 --> 00:22:14.690
You're the one who gave 
me the courage to weave

00:22:14.690 --> 00:22:19.900
So I always want you by my side

00:22:30.550 --> 00:22:34.910
<b>Next Time</b>

00:22:30.550 --> 00:22:34.910
<b>"Ripples"</b>

00:22:38.110 --> 00:22:40.330
Let's hold a press conference!

00:22:41.830 --> 00:22:44.330
Obviously, I feel the same way you do.

00:22:44.330 --> 00:22:47.170
But it will also draw more attention to us.

00:22:47.620 --> 00:22:50.970
It would be a different story if we 
had a powerful attorney on our side.

00:22:51.370 --> 00:22:52.600
I'll do it.

00:22:52.900 --> 00:22:57.320
One wrong word, and they'll 
exaggerate your comment.

00:22:57.320 --> 00:23:00.190
It's no place for a well-meaning amateur.

00:23:00.190 --> 00:23:01.210
But...

00:23:07.110 --> 00:23:08.070
Hi.

00:23:08.930 --> 00:23:09.930
Nagi-san...

00:23:10.810 --> 00:23:14.360
I'll take on that job.

00:23:14.360 --> 00:23:17.330
Here's my new contract.

00:23:15.080 --> 00:23:17.330
<b>Takanashi Productions
Special Publicity Manager Contact</b>

00:23:18.310 --> 00:23:23.330
Takanashi Productions Special 
Publicity Manager Rokuya Nagi?

00:23:23.630 --> 00:23:27.810
Manager, Mr. President.
Let's hold a press conference.

00:23:27.810 --> 00:23:30.710
I'm the one who was holding 
on to Haruki's songs.

00:23:30.710 --> 00:23:32.970
I'm responsible.

00:23:32.970 --> 00:23:35.300
You're going to appear 
at the press conference?

00:23:35.300 --> 00:23:36.330
What are you—

00:23:36.330 --> 00:23:37.830
Don't worry.

00:23:37.830 --> 00:23:43.600
While in my home country, I held regular 
conferences with the citizens once a month.

00:23:43.860 --> 00:23:45.480
Citizens?

00:23:45.480 --> 00:23:49.860
I am also boiling with rage over Haruki.

00:23:49.860 --> 00:23:52.910
I will not allow them to call him a traitor.

00:23:53.270 --> 00:23:59.270
I shall turn the buzzing media
 into a flock of sheep.
